From 16d656fae79020e1b35f85c7180cf8ac7d2f3f09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:22:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/40] generate: STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP=1 reads a batch
 admission's prompt beside the pipelined slot groups

With STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP=1, a pipelined batch (a layer split, more than one slot group) now reads each batched prompt
segment that passes the gate and overlap_prepare (2257db30) on a thread of its own (read_overlapped): sp.run over the
same chunks as before, while the request thread keeps the groups decoding (pump) and applies BSTOPs. The groups in
flight are drained before the read returns, so the checkpoint, header windows, first window and slot copy run as
before. Env off: the same code path as before (pump's pick loop restructured, its all-idle block factored out as
idle_report(true), one row counter; nothing else runs).

- pump while a read runs (ov_active): no pending swap applied; the all-idle line waits for the read's end and leaves
  the watchdog's busy flag alone (idle_report(false) after the drain); a group starts only on a layout every stage has
  captured (ov_layout): its own width, else the full width captured by overlap_prepare (padded up: the extra rows are
  pad rows, sl.cached cleared), else it waits until the read ends. No capture runs beside a read.
- read_overlapped: an RAII guard ends the read thread on every way out (an exception included); on an abort it sets
  stop_req, releases every stage's GPU waits (release_gpu_waits) and gives the read STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP_JOIN_S
  (default 30 s) to end, else _Exit(1). The read thread catches every exception and then joins the stage chain
  (Prefill::join_chain: run() joins it only when it returns). A failed window keeps pump's ERR and text; the caller's
  second ERR is skipped (ov_err_printed). A CUDA error the read's threads saw (their own error state, and
  chain_cuda_error) skips the drain and leads to #224's exit (ov_cuda_fault). An exception out of the loop answers
  one ERR and ends the request as a failed window does.
- the read's own heartbeat: every stage's finished chunk beats; with none for STRATA_WATCHDOG_S during a read (the
  windows' beats hide it from the watchdog) the engine reports the stall, answers ERR and aborts as above, with a
  watchdog allowance for the bounded abort.
- control lines during the read: BSTOP applied, BYIELD dropped (a pipelined read never gave way); the main loop no
  longer drains the groups for a BYIELD (env on only).
- the stats line per read: "strata batch: overlapped read of N tokens in X ms (drain Y ms); the slots decoded R rows
  meanwhile, D_ref ... rows/s, lost Z ms of decode; P group starts padded up, W waited; stage-1 PLE gather ... ms avg
  over K windows, ple hit ...". D_ref is the slots' rate between an admission and the next BGEN (an EMA); lost =
  read+drain - rows / D_ref. The gather time is counted only with set_ple_urgent (Verifier::ms_ple_urgent); the hit
  rate only in Direct mode (n/a with --ple-io ram). STRATA_TRACE=1 also logs each read's start.
- knobs: STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP_SLEEP_US (default 20, 0 = yield) between two turns of the loop; debug only (read when
  the env is on): STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP_FORCE_PADUP=1, STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP_FORCE_WAIT=1|2 (2: a group narrower than the
  full width waits too), STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP_TEST_FAULT=poll|throw|stage|stall (fault paths a, b, c, e).
- tools/batch_overlap_test.py: 14 background slots decode while prompts of ~200, ~1.3K and ~5K tokens (one with a
  root checkpoint: two segments) are admitted, with a slot reuse, a BSTOP and a BYIELD during a read, and a STOP of
  the admitted request during its read; every request must equal its solo tokens; --compare (another run's dump),
  --split, --env, --expect-fault; the log must show the reads' stats lines and no capture inside a read.

Checked (T16-mmqtab.json, STRATA_MMQ_DIRECT=1, --pcie-frac 0 --adapt-every 1000000 --no-prefill-borrow,
STRATA_IQ_MT_MIN=1): batch_overlap_test passes on split 12,24,36 with the env on, off, the reference engine
(strata-g3-mmqtab), FORCE_PADUP=1 and FORCE_WAIT=2, all token-identical; on 13,25,37 env on and off, identical. Env on:
20 overlapped reads per run, none refused, no 'not captured', no capture between a read's start and its stats line;
123 group starts padded up in the plain run (natural layouts such as 12,13,14 not yet captured), 278 with FORCE_PADUP,
21 waits with FORCE_WAIT=2. Faults poll, throw, stage and stall (WATCHDOG_S=10, JOIN_S=2): exactly one ERR, the
engine ends by itself in 5-6 s, no watchdog, no std::terminate. A CUDA fault on the prompt side (fault d) has no
injection hook and is not tested. First numbers (not M4's): a 1.27K-token read takes ~835 ms beside 14 slots (609 ms
drained) and loses ~440 ms of decode; ~200-token reads 250-340 ms (200 ms).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
